vault.kit.text:
CloudDrives - recovery kit for the vault "{0}"
Created on {1} on the PC {2}

Account:              {3} ({4})
Cloud folder:         {5}
Password:             {6}
Salt:                 {7}

Without password AND salt the files in the vault are lost forever -
neither CloudDrives nor the provider can recover them.
Keep both safe (password manager or printout), never unencrypted in the cloud.

On another PC: CloudDrives > Manage drives > Add drive > Encrypted vault,
choose the same folder and enter password and salt.

Access without CloudDrives, with rclone only (https://rclone.org):
rclone config create my-vault crypt remote="YOUR-ACCOUNT:{5}" password="{6}" password2="{7}" filename_encryption=standard directory_name_encryption=true filename_encoding={8} --obscure
